data.content:
Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc`'d `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`. Tested on .NET 11 (preview) and it works perfectly:

```csharp
Span<nint>  nints  = stackalloc nint[4];
Span<nuint> nuints = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

Both native-sized integer types (`nint` / `nuint`, introduced in C# 9) are valid `stackalloc` targets. They're 8 bytes each on this 64-bit system, as confirmed by `nint.MaxValue` being `9223372036854775807` (Int64.MaxValue).

